@startuml D-Fence-Architecture
' D-Fence — System architecture (Lab 3 deliverable 2, part 3)
' Subsystem decomposition and deployment, per Bruegge ch. 6 and 7.
' Style: three-tier client/server with a separate scheduling process.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

node "Browser (Chrome / Edge / Safari)\n360-1920 px, 10.7.1, 10.7.2" as Browser {
  component "D-Fence Web Client\nReact 18 + TypeScript + Vite" as Client {
    component "Screens (27)\n<<boundary>>" as Screens
    component "Route Guard\nrole -> permitted region" as Guard
    component "API Client\nfetch + query cache" as ApiClient
    component "Map View\nLeaflet + OneMap tiles" as MapView
  }
}

node "Application Server\nNode 20 + Express + TypeScript" as AppServer {
  component "HTTP Boundary\nroute handlers, DTO validation\n<<boundary>>" as Routes
  component "Access Control\nAccessControlService (2.3.6)\n<<control>>" as AC
  component "Domain Services\n15 control classes\n<<control>>" as Services
  component "Domain Model\n23 entity classes\n<<entity>>" as Domain
  component "Persistence\nrepositories + SQL\nin-memory stores\n<<persistence>>" as Persistence
  component "External Gateways\n5 adapters\n<<boundary>>" as Gateways
}

node "Scheduler Process\nnode-cron, same image" as Scheduler {
  component "Ingestion Jobs\nrainfall 5 min, clusters hourly,\nforecast 6 h, token 48 h" as Jobs
}

database "PostgreSQL 15 + PostGIS\n(Supabase)" as DB {
  component "Relational tables\n+ spatial indexes" as Tables
  component "Row-Level Security\ndefence in depth" as RLS
}

cloud "Supabase managed services" as SupaCloud {
  component "Supabase Auth\ncredentials, verification,\nreset links, sessions" as SupaAuth
  component "Supabase Storage\nreport + evidence photos\nprivate buckets only" as Storage
}

cloud "External data sources" as External {
  component "NEA dengue clusters\nGeoJSON" as NEA
  component "data.gov.sg rainfall\n5-min, 97 stations" as Rain
  component "data.gov.sg 24 h forecast\n5 macro-regions" as Forecast
  component "OneMap\nSearch + tiles, 3-day token" as OneMap
  component "Telegram Bot API" as Telegram
}

Screens --> Guard
Guard --> ApiClient
MapView --> ApiClient
ApiClient --> Routes : HTTPS / JSON (10.3.2)
MapView ..> OneMap : tile requests (browser-direct)

Routes --> AC : authorise every request
AC --> Services
Routes --> Services
Services --> Domain
Services --> Persistence
Persistence --> Tables
Persistence --> RLS
Services --> Gateways
Services --> Storage : signed, non-enumerable URLs (10.3.5)
Services --> SupaAuth : register, sign in, reset (2.1.x)
Routes --> SupaAuth : verify bearer token

Jobs --> Services : IngestionController, PriorityScoringEngine,\nAlertTriggerEvaluator
Gateways --> NEA
Gateways --> Rain
Gateways --> Forecast
Gateways --> OneMap
Gateways --> Telegram

note right of Scheduler
  A separate process, not a timer inside the web
  server. Two reasons: 10.2.3 requires ingestion to
  resume automatically after a restart, which is
  simpler when scheduling is not tied to request
  serving; and a slow ingestion cycle must not
  consume the request threads that 10.1.2 and
  10.1.5 constrain.
end note

note bottom of AC
  Every request passes through here before any
  service runs. 2.3.6 and 10.3.3 require server-side
  enforcement; RLS in the database is the second
  layer, not the first, because the requirement is
  about the server, not the store.
  Supabase Auth authenticates — it answers "who is
  this". Authorisation, "may they", stays here: §2.3
  is written per role, and the role is ours.
end note

note bottom of Persistence
  Repository layer. Spatial predicates (ST_Contains,
  ST_DWithin, ST_Distance) execute in the database,
  not in application code: 1.2.5, 3.1.8 and 5.1.7 are
  nearest-neighbour and point-in-polygon queries.
end note

@enduml
